-- title:
--   Closed convex hulls of nested weakly compact sets
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals.
--
--   1. **Nested compact sets.** A decreasing sequence of nonempty weakly compact sets has a nonempty compact intersection.
--   2. **Support bound.** If $x\in\overline{\mathrm{conv}}\,B$ for a nonempty weakly compact $B$, then every $f\in X^*$ has some $z\in B$ with $f(x)\le f(z)$.
--   3. **Hull of the intersection.** If $x\in\overline{\mathrm{conv}}\,B_n$ for every member of a decreasing sequence of nonempty weakly compact sets, then
--   $$
--   x\in\overline{\mathrm{conv}}\Bigl(\bigcap_nB_n\Bigr),
--   $$
--   by Hahn–Banach separation and compactness of half-space cuts.
